<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Severe aplastic anemia: pancytopenia with a low reticulocyte count, confirmed by a hypocellular bone marrow; attributed to cumulative occupational ionizing radiation; linked to the documented 1934 diagnosis: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Occupational exposure to ionizing radiation over decades of radium research and X-ray work: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Posterior capsule opacification, right eye, after earlier bilateral cataract surgery; glare and blurred reading vision: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Chronic radiodermatitis of the fingertips, with thin, scarred skin: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Medication: continued without change, Cyclosporine (modified) 100 mg oral capsule, one capsule twice daily, dose adjusted to trough levels by hematology [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Eltrombopag 75 mg oral tablet, two tablets (150 mg) once daily on an empty stomach [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Acyclovir 400 mg oral tablet, one tablet twice daily during immunosuppression [S]</item><item>Goal: Hematology evaluation with bone marrow biopsy within one week of the pancytopenia result. Outcome by 2026-05-18: Seen and biopsied seven days after the first visit [S]</item><item>Goal: No serious infection or bleeding during the first months of treatment. Outcome by 2026-06-29: No infection or bleeding through the sixth week of therapy [S]</item><item>Goal: Early rise in neutrophil and platelet counts by the six-week visit. Outcome by 2026-06-29: Neutrophils rose from 0.4 to 0.8 and platelets from 18 to 34 thousand per microliter; formal response is judged at three to six months [S]</item><item>Goal: Read standard print comfortably with the right eye after capsulotomy. Outcome by 2026-06-29: Reading without glare one week after laser capsulotomy [S]</item><item>Continue the care plan agreed on 2026-05-11 [S]</item><item>Scheduled episode complete. Continue routine follow-up [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>
